{"name":"Monet Magic","hex":"#c1acc3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of rituals or actions, especially those based on occult knowledge, to subdue or manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces in order to have some benefit from them. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The supernatural forces which are drawn on in such a ritual."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.","Producing extraordinary results, as though through the use of magic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Claude Monet","blocks":[{"text":"Oscar-Claude Monet was a French painter and founder of Impressionism who is seen as a key precursor to modernism, especially in his attempts to paint nature as he perceived it. During his long career, he was the most consistent and prolific practitioner of Impressionism's philosophy of expressing one's perceptions of nature, especially as applied to plein air (outdoor) landscape painting. The term \"Impressionism\" is derived from the title of his painting Impression, Sunrise, which was exhibited in 1874 at the First Impressionist Exhibition, initiated by Monet and a number of like-minded artists as an alternative to the Salon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Claude_Monet_1899_Nadar_crop.jpg/330px-Claude_Monet_1899_Nadar_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Monet","wikidata":"Q296"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG/500px-Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG/1280px-Claude_Monet_-_Camille.JPG?utm_sour